---
// src/pages/refunds.astro — Refund Policy. Static content page, zero JS.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro'
---

<Base
  title="Refund Policy"
  description="Root My Android's refund policy: cryptocurrency payments are irreversible; Nitro purchases are final with narrow exceptions."
>
  <div class="container prose" style="padding: 3rem 1.25rem">
    <h1>Refund Policy</h1>
    <p class="faint"><em>Last updated: October 20, 2026</em></p>

    <h2>1. Cryptocurrency payments</h2>
    <p>
      Payments to Root My Android are made in cryptocurrency (or, when offered, via a third-party
      on-ramp that converts card / Apple Pay payments to cryptocurrency on our behalf).
      Cryptocurrency transactions are <strong>irreversible by design</strong> — once confirmed on
      the network, they cannot be charged back or recalled.
    </p>

    <h2>2. Nitro purchases</h2>
    <p>
      Nitro purchases are <strong>final</strong>. Nitro is a prepaid credit with no cash or
      cryptocurrency value and is not redeemable outside the Service (see our
      <a href="/terms">Terms of Service</a>). We will, however, make things right when the fault
      is ours:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Credit never arrived</strong> — if your payment confirmed but the Nitro was not
        credited, contact us with the payment ID or transaction hash and your account number; we
        will credit it manually.</li>
      <li><strong>Duplicate charge</strong> — an accidental duplicate payment for the same order
        will be re-credited as Nitro or returned in the original cryptocurrency, at our
        discretion.</li>
      <li><strong>Service failure</strong> — if a PRO feature consumed Nitro but failed due to a
        defect on our side, the Nitro will be re-credited.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>3. Voucher codes</h2>
    <p>
      Voucher (redeem) codes are non-refundable once redeemed. Unredeemed codes purchased from an
      authorized reseller are subject to that reseller's own refund terms.
    </p>

    <h2>4. Free tier</h2>
    <p>
      Device scanning, guides, and the ROM catalog are free. No payment means nothing to refund —
      but if something is broken, we still want to hear about it.
    </p>

    <h2>5. How to request</h2>
    <p>
      Email <a href="mailto:support@rootmyandroid.com">support@rootmyandroid.com</a> with your
      16-digit account number and the payment ID or transaction hash. We aim to respond within 5
      business days.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
